    glossary: `
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li><b>Armadillo (Dasypus novemcinctus):</b> Natural non-human animal reservoir for <i>M. leprae</i> in the southern United States.</li>
        <li><b>ENL (Erythema Nodosum Leprosum):</b> Type III immune-complex reaction in multibacillary leprosy presenting with painful dermal nodules, fever, and uveitis.</li>
        <li><b>Fite-Faraco Stain:</b> Modified carbolfuchsin acid-fast stain utilizing peanut oil to prevent over-decolorization of <i>M. leprae</i>.</li>
        <li><b>Globi:</b> Compact, rounded microscopic clumps of hundreds of <i>M. leprae</i> bacilli packed parallel inside lipid histiocytes.</li>
        <li><b>Hansen Disease:</b> Proper clinical medical term for leprosy, honoring Gerhard Armauer Hansen.</li>
        <li><b>Leonine Facies:</b> Characteristic facial distortion in lepromatous leprosy caused by diffuse nodular thickening of eyebrows, nose, and earlobes.</li>
        <li><b>Lepromin Test:</b> Skin test measuring delayed hypersensitivity to lepra antigens; positive in tuberculoid, negative in lepromatous.</li>
        <li><b>Paucibacillary:</b> Classification characterized by 1 to 5 skin lesions with absent or rare acid-fast bacilli on slit smears.</li>
        <li><b>PGL-1 (Phenolic Glycolipid-1):</b> Unique surface trisaccharide glycolipid mediating specific attachment to Schwann cell laminin-2.</li>
        <li><b>Schwann Cell:</b> Principal glia of the peripheral nervous system; primary cellular target of <i>M. leprae</i> invasion and demyelinating injury.</li>
        <li><b>Virchow Cells:</b> Foamy, lipid-engorged histiocytes/macrophages packed with bacilli in lepromatous tissue.</li>
      </ul>
    `
